  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="12">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VAtr">V Atr</ref> 12</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-g">⁊ saulsceat is rihtast, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> man symle gelæste æt openu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> græfe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-g2">⁊ saulsceat is rihtas, þæt man symle gelæste á æt openum græfe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="12" corresp="#wit-d">⁊ sawlsceatt is rihtast þæt man symle gelæste æt openum græfe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">And it is best that payment for the souls of the dead should always be rendered before the grave is closed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und Seelengeld ist am richtigsten, dass man immer [sofort] zahle bei offenem Grabe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And as for soul-scot, it is most right that it always be paid [at once] at the open grave.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">G2's ‘rihtas’ should be corrected to ‘rihtast’.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
